<h2 id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-version_history1.1VersionHist=
ory"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;Mas=
kingDesign-version_history"></span>1.1 Version History</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 73=
.1237%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 8.56796%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 13.0423%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 15.4223%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 63.0221%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Version</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Version Date</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Revised By</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">0.1</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><time datetime=3D"2025-10-17" class=3D"date-past">17 Oct 2025</tim=
e>&nbsp;</p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <a class=3D"confluence-userlink user-mention" data-username=3D"943761=
" href=3D"/display/~943761" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1371341939" data-lin=
ked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"userinfo" data-base=
-url=3D"https://confluence.nz.thenational.com">Bradley Freedman</a>&nbsp;
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">First Draft of document ready for review</td=
>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">0.2</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><time datetime=3D"2025-11-05" class=3D"date-past">05 Nov 2025</tim=
e>&nbsp;</p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><a class=3D"confluence-userlink user-mention" data-username=3D"943=
761" href=3D"/display/~943761" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1371341939" data-=
linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"userinfo" data-b=
ase-url=3D"https://confluence.nz.thenational.com">Bradley Freedman</a>&nbsp=
;</p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>The following changes have been applied to the document as part of =
Review Cycle 1, ready for Review Cycle 2.&nbsp;</p>
     <ul>
      <li>Section 4.3 - Scope Clarifications=20
       <ul>
        <li>Item 3: Added a new Out of Scope item titled Classification Rul=
es. Clarified that the determination and definition of classification rules=
 for data attributes are outside the scope of this solution. These rules wi=
ll be established collaboratively by Alation, the designated Data Steward, =
and the Data Management &amp; Governance (DM&amp;G) team.</li>
        <li>Item 4: Revised language to explain why automatic propagation o=
f classifications from the System of Record (SoR) is out of scope for Alati=
on. To ensure consistency, the same Catalogue Set used to classify the SoR =
will also be used to scan and apply classifications within Snowflake, treat=
ing Snowflake as another SoR governed by the same classification logic. Thi=
s is further detailed in Section 9.1 Appendix Item 2: How Alation Scans and=
 Applies Classifications.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 8.3.4 - Alation Analytics Support=20
       <ul>
        <li>Added new documentation outlining the Alation Analytics SLA and=
 Support Agreements, detailing how incidents, responsibilities, and support=
 interactions are managed between Alation, BNZ, and Snowflake.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 8.3.5 - Alation Analytics Change Management=20
       <ul>
        <li>Introduced a new subsection describing the Alation Analytics ch=
ange management process, including how structural changes to alation analyt=
ics tables and schemas are communicated and managed to minimize downstream =
impact.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 8.5.1 - Key Classifications That Will Inform Data Masking=
&nbsp;=20
       <ul>
        <li>Rule 1: Determine when to mask or hash data to account for Busi=
ness Keys, Primary Keys and Foreign Keys.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 8.5.4 - Handling of Business, Primary and Foreign Keys=20
       <ul>
        <li>Handling of Business Keys, Primary Keys and Foreign Keys update=
d to document design decisions, in addition to alternatives considered.</li=
>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 8.5.5 - Classification Edge Case Handling=20
       <ul>
        <li>Added clarification on how both Alation and Snowflake handle ed=
ge cases where multiple classifications may apply to a data element.</li>
        <li>Documented the approach for resolving overlaps when classificat=
ions are derived from different Catalogue Sets.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 8.6.1 - Landing Zone Structure and Access Controls=20
       <ul>
        <li>Expanded documentation describing how the Landing Zone is divid=
ed into two conceptual areas: General Landing Zone: For the majority of dat=
a sources &amp; Restricted Landing Zone: For data sources with heightened s=
ensitivity.</li>
        <li>Defined the =E2=80=98Restricted Access=E2=80=99 role within the=
 Landing Zone, which enforces additional controls and limits visibility to =
a small group of privileged Landing Developers.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>Section 9.2 - Appendix Item 2=20
       <ul>
        <li>Added a new appendix titled =E2=80=9CHow Alation Scans Snowflak=
e and Applies Classifications=E2=80=9D, describing the scanning process and=
 classification application across both the Analytical and Operational plan=
es.</li>
       </ul></li>
      <li>General Updates=20
       <ul>
        <li>Minor revisions to grammar, language, and formatting throughout=
 the document to improve readability and consistency.</li>
       </ul></li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">0.3</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><time datetime=3D"2025-11-25" class=3D"date-past">25 Nov 2025</tim=
e>&nbsp;</p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><a class=3D"confluence-userlink user-mention" data-username=3D"943=
761" href=3D"/display/~943761" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1371341939" data-=
linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"userinfo" data-b=
ase-url=3D"https://confluence.nz.thenational.com">Bradley Freedman</a>&nbsp=
;</p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>The following changes have been applied to the document as part of =
Review Cycle 2, prior to submission for endorsement.</p>
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"face760d-6a6e-49d6-9e61-4663207a30c7">Section 4.1 - =
Open Items=20
       <ul>
        <li data-uuid=3D"d792356e-9eea-4b95-a719-1471b71c809a">Item 3: Pote=
ntial inclusion of Snowflake NON-PROD environment as part of this design.</=
li>
       </ul></li>
     </ul></td>
