<p><sup>Upon endorsement of this document, the detailed list of AD Group Na=
mes and how they map to the Snowflake Roles at a Zone Level will be updated=
. A reference to to this document is provided&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-lin=
k" href=3D"https://bnz.sharepoint.com/:x:/t/DataAITransformationProgramme2/=
EcimQJNCOnFIlkjRD2YNm0cBkwU5gi5bWRUcCftUMnKc0g?email=3DBradley_Freedman%40b=
nz.co.nz&amp;e=3DwG4AZk&amp;clickparams=3DeyAiWC1BcHBOYW1lIiA6ICJNaWNyb3NvZ=
nQgT3V0bG9vayIsICJYLUFwcFZlcnNpb24iIDogIjE2LjAuMTkwMjkuMjAyNDQiLCAiT1MiIDog=
IldpbmRvd3MiIH0%3D&amp;CID=3D1722F303-D210-474D-98B3-FD43FE12D1EA&amp;wdLOR=
=3Dc8A801A9A-9F7F-4BDC-8D75-488A08636B31" rel=3D"nofollow">here</a>.&nbsp;&=
nbsp;</sup></p>
<h3 id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-transform_db8.6.2RoleBasedSpe=
cificallyForDeveloperRoleWithinTRANSFORMDatabase"><span class=3D"confluence=
-anchor-link" id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-transform_db"></spa=
n>8.6.2 Role Based Specifically For Developer Role Within TRANSFORM Databas=
e</h3>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"5e57a294-5008-495f-ae2=
5-f77d7cf004d0">As documented in </span><a href=3D"https://confluence.nz.th=
enational.com/display/BAI/BDH+sub-design+-+Foundations" rel=3D"nofollow"><s=
pan class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"5e57a294-5008-495f-ae25-f77=
d7cf004d0">BDH sub-design - Foundations - Digital, Data &amp; Analytics - B=
NZ Confluence</span></a><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"5=
e57a294-5008-495f-ae25-f77d7cf004d0"> under section '[ZONE]__TRANSFORM__DEV=
', this is a special database that exists only in DEV. This enables develop=
ment and end-to-end unit testing without raising conflicts with other devel=
oper's object execution during unit testing.</span></p>
<p>Every object built locally in dbt core, before it is executed in Astrono=
mer, is created within a named schema under this database. Every developer =
will have a schema named after the developer, typically the BNZ User ID.</p=
>
<p>This allows developers to run end-to-end upstream and downstream models =
to perform complete validation without it affecting objects in the other da=
ta layers such as RAW/FOUNDATION/CURATED. Importantly, once initial access =
is granted to the LANDING database, the developer can rapidly build data pr=
oducts within the Transform Database without any new data products being au=
to-classified, given the schema is restricted against every unique develope=
r. This means that developers with access to '<em>Highly Confidential'</em>=
 data will be able to developer data products within the Transformation Dat=
abase within their own restricted schema; no other developer even with the =
'Highly Confidential', 'Confidential' or 'Private' role will have access to=
 another developer's schema. Given the data is restricted to the developer'=
s unique schema, <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"b36a252d=
-9811-4a3c-ad6f-cd1829e37076">development of data products</span> can occur=
 rapidly.</p>
<p>When objects are deployed via Astronomer to the other data layers, these=
 are <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"5dd9d343-81db-4a29-a=
6dd-65d56682e8d5">created accordingly i</span>n RAW/FOUNDATION/CURATED. As =
described in previous sections, Default Classification is applied and then =
updated once the Alation Classifications become available.</p>
<p>The override macros that define where objects are created from dbt (gene=
rate_alias_name, generate_database_name and generate_schema_name) have been=
 refactored to consider this.</p>
<p>As a result, developers do not need to specify this explicitly in the db=
t project configuration to differentiate the behavior in dbt and can simply=
 follow the naming conventions required for a model to make this work for b=
oth TRANSFORM database as well as its final materialization in RAW/FOUNDATI=
ON/CURATED.</p>
<p>For further reading, please refer to the following document: <a href=3D"=
/spaces/BAI/pages/1570472785/List+of+Macros+their+detailed+Specifications">=
List of Macros &amp; their detailed Specifications</a>.&nbsp;To help illust=
rate this solution the following diagram can be referenced:</p>
<p><map id=3D"gliffy-map-1999700588-7798" name=3D"gliffy-map-1999700588-779=
8"></map></p>
<table width=3D"100%" class=3D"gliffy-macro-table">
 <tbody>
  <tr>
   <td>
    <table class=3D"gliffy-macro-inner-table">
     <caption align=3D"bottom">
     </caption>
     <tbody>
      <tr>
       <td><img style=3D"border: none; width: 600px;" usemap=3D"#gliffy-map=
-1999700588-7798" src=3D"b6253096c4c7d7606935998f9798f73f9532d5d5eafbbea60f=
5509b048cbb4c1" alt=3D"" class=3D"gliffy-macro-image" width=3D"468" height=
=3D"291"></td>
      </tr>
     </tbody>
    </table></td>
  </tr>
 </tbody>
</table>
<br>
<br><strong>To Support The Classification and Masking Solution, the followi=
ng RBAC changes will be required:</strong>
<p></p>
<ol>
 <li>RBAC changes that ensure developer schemas are accessible only to the =
developer after which the schema is named.</li>
 <li>Classification and masking is not required within the schema objects, =
as only the developer will be able to access this schema.</li>
 <li>Read access is maintained as specified elsewhere in this document, in =
the sense that it will be based on both the role granted and the access on =
landing read according to the zone's requirements.</li>
</ol>
<p><span><span>&nbsp;<br></span></span><strong>Note: </strong>RBAC changes =
required will be enabled via the Automation and RBAC framework:</p>
<ol>
 <li>As part of onboarding a developer, the schema is added to the Automati=
on configuration, appropriate RBAC configurations made and the pipeline is =
executed.</li>
 <li>As part of offboarding a developer, all schemas that relate to the dev=
eloper must be dropped (by removing the config line) and managed via the Au=
tomation and RBAC pipeline. Automation pipeline needs to be enhanced to sup=
port this.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
<p>The responsibility of onboarding and offboarding the developer, will lie=
 with the RBAC Admin identified for the Zone once the Platform is handed ov=
er to the Zone Engineering and Admin team.</p>
<h1 id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-9.Appendix">9. Appendix</h1>
<h2 id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-section_9.19.1AppendixItem1-K=
DD01DataClassificationOptionsandRoleofAlation"><span class=3D"confluence-an=
chor-link" id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-section_9.1"></span>9.=
1 Appendix Item 1 - KDD01 Data Classification Options and Role of Alation</=
h2>
<p><strong>Context:</strong> The following section describes the role of Al=
ation and how this will be used to provide 'classification instructions' to=
 Snowflake where data masking rules will be applied. There are multiple way=
s these 'instructions' can be provided; these are documented below.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 95=
.6044%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 8.13556%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 21.4251%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 22.9159%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 22.6603%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 24.8312%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Option #</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Option Name</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Pros</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Cons</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;"><span class=3D"status-macro aui-loz=
enge aui-lozenge-success">OPTION 1</span></span><br><br><em><span class=3D"=
inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"3f98edba-64cb-4b9c-b8a0-29b4e333eaa4">Se=
lected Option</span></em></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>Data classification instructions provided early in data lifecycle =
via Alation NON-PROD and Snowflake DEV<br><br><strong><br><br><map id=3D"gl=
iffy-map-1968704286-1206" name=3D"gliffy-map-1968704286-1206"></map> </stro=
ng></p>
      <table width=3D"100%" class=3D"gliffy-macro-table">
       <tbody>
        <tr>
         <td>
          <table class=3D"gliffy-macro-inner-table">
           <caption align=3D"bottom">
           </caption>
           <tbody>
            <tr>
             <td><img style=3D"border: none; width: 300px;" usemap=3D"#glif=
fy-map-1968704286-1206" src=3D"03f0e32e82504bdd40d55b18c3494d91b206cb6a6895=
d55c018f3c70396a4bb9" alt=3D"" class=3D"gliffy-macro-image" width=3D"468" h=
eight=3D"134"></td>
            </tr>
           </tbody>
          </table></td>
        </tr>
       </tbody>
      </table><strong> <br></strong>
      <p></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Alation NON-PROD sources will be used to scan DEV <u>and</u> clas=
sify tables in lower environments</li>
      <li>The classification of tables within Snowflake DEV will enable the=
 Alation Tag Value to be set for individual table field values. This can al=
so automated using Alation NON-PROD catalog&nbsp;set.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>
       <p>A single collection of Alation NON-PROD data source will be lever=
aged to classify values after scanning data from Snowflake DEV. This same N=
ON-PROD data source will serve as the central reference for classifications=
, which will then be applied consistently across Snowflake DEV, SYST, and P=
PTE lower environments</p></li>
      <li>A single collection of Alation PROD data source will be leveraged=
 to classify values after scanning data from Snowflake PROD. This same PROD=
 data source will serve as the central reference for classifications within=
 the PROD environment.</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Alation provides a UI to the business to automate or apply manual=
 tagging to data objects within Snowflake.</li>
      <li>Promotes consistency through environments by persisting and promo=
ting tag values within Alation.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Reduces duplication of classification effort across all other Sno=
wflake environments (SYST, PPTE, PROD)&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Data in higher environments (SYST, PPTE, PROD) is immediately mas=
ked once objects are deployed into these environments.</li>
      <li>Promotes early stewardship and governance of data early in the da=
ta product lifecycle.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>In the event, NON-PROD source system test data is not available, =
this solution enables enables the ability to use <span class=3D"inline-comm=
ent-marker" data-ref=3D"c92b6040-248a-493c-92aa-de81d3cad01e">PROD data giv=
en classification &amp; masking to occur directly in Snowflake (DEV), subje=
ct to other guardrails and approvals.</span>&nbsp;</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Alation PROD cannot re-classify data directly in Snowflake PROD; =
these re-classifications must be applied via Alation DEV in addition to re-=
publishing the Snowflake objects via the deployment pipeline.</li>
      <li>Increased data engineering complexities as Snowflake Tags need to=
 be persisted prior to promotion to any higher environment. &nbsp;<span>Thi=
s is required to ensure that the macro reapplies tags when the DBT object i=
s rebuilt in a higher environment. </span></li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;"><span class=3D"status-macro aui-loz=
enge aui-lozenge-subtle">OPTION 2</span></span><br><br><br></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>Data classification instructions provided later in data lifecycle =
via Alation PROD and Snowflake PROD<br><br><map id=3D"gliffy-map-1968704282=
-3419" name=3D"gliffy-map-1968704282-3419"></map></p>
      <table width=3D"100%" class=3D"gliffy-macro-table">
       <tbody>
        <tr>
         <td>
          <table class=3D"gliffy-macro-inner-table">
           <caption align=3D"bottom">
           </caption>
           <tbody>
            <tr>
             <td><img style=3D"border: none; width: 300px;" usemap=3D"#glif=
fy-map-1968704282-3419" src=3D"90657757ee50cdc0870cc8bf025ead4d87a9bb32971c=
2962b93238dc632c3c0c" alt=3D"" class=3D"gliffy-macro-image" width=3D"468" h=
eight=3D"134"></td>
            </tr>
           </tbody>
          </table></td>
        </tr>
       </tbody>
      </table>
      <p></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Alation NON-PROD will be treated as a sandpit only and will <u>no=
t</u> be used to &nbsp;to scan&nbsp;<u>and</u> classify tables within Snowf=
lake DEV environment&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Alation PROD to will be used to scan <u>and</u> classify tables w=
ithin Snowflake PROD,&nbsp;</li>
      <li>A single collection of Alation PROD data source will be leveraged=
 to classify values after scanning data from Snowflake PROD. This same PROD=
 data source will serve as the central reference for classifications within=
 the PROD environment.</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Alation provides a UI to the business to automate or apply manual=
 tagging to data objects within Snowflake.</li>
      <li>Decreased data engineering complexity given only a single environ=
ment is maintained.</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Stewardship and governance of data occurs later in data product l=
ifecycle.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Data in lower environments (DEV, SYST, PPTE) is never masked and =
data within PROD will only be masked once Alation scans and classifies the =
data; this might result in delayed time to value to make data available.</l=
i>
      <li>Reduced mechanisms to protect PROD data that is made available in=
to the NON-PROD environment.&nbsp;</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;"><span class=3D"status-macro aui-loz=
enge aui-lozenge-subtle">OPTION 3</span></span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>Data classification instructions provided at all phases in the dat=
a lifecycle across all environments via Alation NON-PROD and Alation PROD<b=
r><br><span> <map id=3D"gliffy-map-1968704284-8377" name=3D"gliffy-map-1968=
704284-8377"></map> </span></p>
      <table width=3D"100%" class=3D"gliffy-macro-table">
       <tbody>
        <tr>
         <td>
          <table class=3D"gliffy-macro-inner-table">
           <caption align=3D"bottom">
           </caption>
           <tbody>
            <tr>
             <td><img style=3D"border: none; width: 300px;" usemap=3D"#glif=
fy-map-1968704284-8377" src=3D"078021b918099ee848e1833931354d169511479cc603=
dece25726e446d843b37" alt=3D"" class=3D"gliffy-macro-image" width=3D"468" h=
eight=3D"133"></td>
            </tr>
           </tbody>
          </table></td>
        </tr>
       </tbody>
      </table>
      <p></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Alation will scan every environment independency (DEV, SYST, PPTE=
, PROD) <u>and</u> classify every environment independently.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>An Alation data source and likely catalog&nbsp;sets will be estab=
lished for every environment.&nbsp;</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Provides granular level control to independently set the classifi=
cations across each environment.</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Significantly increase complexity and resourcing requirements of =
data stewards to manage Alation and scanning of all Snowflake Environments =
(DEV, SYST, PPTE &amp; PROD). Note: this is further extrapolated as each da=
ta layer (i.e.: RAW, LAND, CORE, PRESENT) needs to be scanned in each of th=
ese environments.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Significant risk classification tags are not properly maintained =
across all the environments.</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;"><span class=3D"status-macro aui-loz=
enge aui-lozenge-subtle">OPTION 4</span></span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>Data classification instructions provided early in data lifecycle =
via DBT only. Alation to only be used in PROD and positioned as a data cata=
logue only that is a receiver of metadata<br><br><map id=3D"gliffy-map-1968=
704280-3772" name=3D"gliffy-map-1968704280-3772"></map></p>
      <table width=3D"100%" class=3D"gliffy-macro-table">
       <tbody>
        <tr>
         <td>
          <table class=3D"gliffy-macro-inner-table">
           <caption align=3D"bottom">
           </caption>
           <tbody>
            <tr>
             <td><img style=3D"border: none; width: 300px;" usemap=3D"#glif=
fy-map-1968704280-3772" src=3D"d7d79c2b124253c8846d8c33b718c1824a271cd5df4f=
257f027a8b060d39ba67" alt=3D"" class=3D"gliffy-macro-image" width=3D"468" h=
eight=3D"134"></td>
            </tr>
           </tbody>
          </table></td>
        </tr>
       </tbody>
      </table>
      <p></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Neither Alation NON-PROD or Alation PROD will be used to classify=
 tables within Snowflake environments.</li>
      <li>Instead classification of tables will be set by data engineers di=
rectly via DBT as part of data engineering activities.</li>
      <li>Alation will only be a receiver of metadata&nbsp;</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>Promotes consistency through environments by persisting and promo=
ting tag values from a single Snowflake environment (DEV)</li>
      <li>Reduces duplication of classification effort across all other Sno=
wflake environments (SYST, PPTE, PROD)&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Data in higher environments (SYST, PPTE, PROD) is immediately mas=
ked once objects are deployed into these environments.</li>
      <li>Promotes early stewardship and governance of data early in the da=
ta product lifecycle.&nbsp;</li>
      <li>In the event, NON-PROD source system test data is not available, =
this solution enables enables the ability to use PROD data given classifica=
tion &amp; masking to occur directly in Snowflake (DEV).&nbsp;</li>
      <li>Decreased data engineering complexities as Snowflake Tags are spe=
cified directly by data engineers within DBT code. There is no need to crea=
te separate data engineering solutions to persist tag values that are set b=
y Alation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li>No UI provided to the business to automate or apply manual taggin=
g to data objects within Snowflake.</li>
      <li>Alation PROD cannot re-classify data directly in Snowflake PROD; =
these re-classifications must be applied via Alation DEV in addition to re-=
publishing the Snowflake objects via the deployment pipeline.</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesign-section_9.29.2AppendixItem2-D=
iagramIllustratingHowAlationWillScanSnowflake&amp;ApplyClassifications"><sp=
an class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BDHClassification&amp;MaskingDesi=
gn-section_9.2"></span>9.2 Appendix Item 2 - Diagram Illustrating How Alati=
on Will Scan Snowflake &amp; Apply Classifications</h2>
<p><strong>Context:</strong> The following diagram describes how Alation wi=
ll scan Snowflake and then apply classifications using a defined catalogue =
set within Alation, as opposed to directly inheriting the classifications f=
rom a scanned System of Record (SoR).<br><br><map id=3D"gliffy-map-20313217=
38-9812" name=3D"gliffy-map-2031321738-9812"></map></p>
<table width=3D"100%" class=3D"gliffy-macro-table">
 <tbody>
  <tr>
   <td>
    <table class=3D"gliffy-macro-inner-table">
     <caption align=3D"bottom">
     </caption>
     <tbody>
      <tr>
       <td><img style=3D"border: none; width: 600px;" usemap=3D"#gliffy-map=
-2031321738-9812" src=3D"bd41382aace1db10c4036ee99d1cafb840194f9abd9006ced0=
7e2351ca7e0b17" alt=3D"" class=3D"gliffy-macro-image" width=3D"468" height=
=3D"237"></td>
      </tr>
     </tbody>
    </table></td>
  </tr>
 </tbody>
</table>
